-- 132: THREE TOOLING-HONESTY METHOD RULES (M1/M2/M3), the U-N10 re-scope, and one falsifiable optimisation
-- hypothesis. Follows 117/119/120/122/124/130. Source doc: mvc-live-skins-quarters/docs/SUPERGUN-NETCODE.md s12.
-- Method step 4. Lane numbering: SUPERGUN NETCODE takes EVEN numbers from 120 up.
-- The M-rules are recorded as method rather than as notes on individual nodes, because they are systemic and will
-- recur now that four lanes write to one graph. M3 in particular corrupts EVIDENCE WEIGHT rather than a number.
-- Apply with tools/re_kb/apply_seed.py after the README export backup
-- (re_kb_data/_exports/re_kb_20260904-164254_pre132.surql). Idempotent and order-independent. No apostrophes in literals.
-- Do NOT re-run 07_dedup_edges.surql afterwards.
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:supergun_method_rules_20260904 SET kind='doc', strength='code', ref='mvc-live-skins-quarters/docs/SUPERGUN-NETCODE.md s12; docs/FRAME-READSET.md s1 and s6.3; docs/RECEIPT-RUNNER-GATE-N1.md s1.2; docs/RECEIPT-RUNNER-GATE4.md s1; the runner IAT map d3dcap/receipt/runner iat_map.txt', note='Method rules and a scope correction. The three M-rules were each discovered on 2026-09-04 by a different lane and are one family: a tool that reports a number without reporting its own health invites a confident wrong conclusion.';

UPSERT finding:method_check_instrument_health_before_quoting SET status='confirmed', text='M1. CHECK THE INSTRUMENT BEFORE QUOTING ITS NUMBERS. Concretely for the receipt runner: check heap_wraps in summary.json before quoting any timing. The first N1b emission showed 1 event over the 16.667 ms budget at depth 120 (max 18.31 ms) and an 11.78 ms outlier at depth 60; both were the runner OWN bump heap WRAPPING, because a resim consumes it depth+1 times faster and a wrap memsets up to 64 MiB inside a single tick. heap_wraps read exactly 1 at those two depths and 0 everywhere else, so the outliers were the instrument and not the engine. --heap-mb now sizes the heap and the driver scripts pass 1024. GENERALISED: every harness in this project that reports a measurement must also report its own health counters, and no number may be quoted until those counters have been read. The failure this prevents is the most expensive kind, because an instrument artefact that looks like a real deadline miss will be designed around.';

UPSERT finding:method_seed_replay_failures_are_relate_artefacts SET status='confirmed', text='M2. A NON-ZERO failed COUNT WHEN RE-APPLYING A SEED IS NORMALLY A RELATE ARTEFACT, NOT A FAILURE. Observed re-applying seeds 117, 119, 122, 124 and 130: UPSERT nodes and UPDATE fields converge idempotently, but explicit-id RELATE edges error with Database record already exists, so a replay reports e.g. 40 statements, 11 failed while the graph is fully correct. READ THE MESSAGES BEFORE TREATING THE COUNT AS A PROBLEM: classify them (grep the -> lines) and confirm they are all already exists. The failure this prevents is someone concluding a seed did not land and re-deriving settled work, or worse, editing the graph by hand to fix a non-problem. A seed that is genuinely order-dependent is a different matter: see the seed 119 and 120 case where a replay WOULD have regressed richer notes until both seeds were made to carry identical strings.';

UPSERT finding:method_derived_finding_is_not_independent_confirmation SET status='confirmed', text='M3. A FINDING DERIVED FROM ANOTHER LANE MEASUREMENT IS NOT AN INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION, AND MUST SAY SO. Two graph nodes citing one underlying measurement read as two confirmations to anyone counting support, which is a FALSE CORROBORATION. With four lanes writing to one graph this recurs by construction: it happened the same day when seeds 128 (research lane) and 130 (netcode lane) independently recorded the same two conclusions -- server authority loses on latency, and pin-and-isolate is required -- from the same arithmetic and the same single tenancy measurement. THE RULE: a finding that consumes another lane result must (a) RELATE ...->cites-> the ORIGINAL FINDING and not merely the shared source, (b) state explicitly what it ADDS beyond the original, and (c) carry a NOT AN INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION -- CITE ONE, NOT BOTH marker in its note. Applied retroactively to finding:supergun_server_authority_ruled_out and finding:supergun_pin_and_isolate. This is the rule with teeth of the three, because M1 and M2 corrupt a number while M3 corrupts EVIDENCE WEIGHT -- and a knowledge graph is precisely the artefact people consult in order to judge how well supported a claim is.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_render_budget_unknown SET status='open', text='U-N10, RE-SCOPED 2026-09-04 (supersedes the seed-130 wording, which called the whole render budget unknown). CONFIRMED and verified rather than accepted: FRAME-READSET s1 states that FUN_140607d60 runs the whole frame and that its top-level calls are FUN_1408441d0, FUN_140608a00 (sim) and FUN_14060b960, the render table loop (dispatcher FUN_140620960, FUN_1406185e0 twice, FUN_140845130), so tick means sim plus render dispatch plus sprite walker plus NaomiLib submit, and render means the dispatcher alone. FUN_140607d60 is wrapped by FUN_140118950, which is exactly what this lane times, SO THE MEASURED 0.034 TO 0.039 ms p50 ALREADY CONTAINS THE GEOMETRY AND DRAW-LIST WALK AND THE SUBMIT. ONE CORRECTION TO THE SUPPORTING ARGUMENT: it is tempting to argue that the runner traps 252 IAT slots with 0 hits over 380 ticks and therefore makes no graphics call inside the tick, but THAT ARGUMENT DOES NOT HOLD -- the trapped slice 0x1408db000..0x1408db880 is 257 slots containing 132 KERNEL32, 13 ntdll and 112 unresolved, and NO d3d11 or dxgi entries at all, so a zero-hit result over a slice that does not cover graphics imports says nothing about graphics imports. What actually supports the split is weaker in kind and is tagged accordingly: the runner executes 300 plus ticks BYTE-EXACTLY WITH NO GRAPHICS DEVICE AT ALL, and the tick render output is host-memory fills into *(game_state+0x208) (texture staging) and dev+0xD8D04 (PALETTE_RAM) rather than API calls -- INFERRED strong, not proven. THE RE-SCOPED UNKNOWN IS THEREFORE: the CPU cost of turning the NaomiLib staging buffers into draw calls, plus Present overhead and the input poll, i.e. everything in the frame that is NOT inside FUN_140118950. That is bounded and much smaller than render, and the render lane can upper-bound it from the existing browser replay path. CONSEQUENCE FOR THE CAP: at depth 60 the worst measured frame is 5.93 ms leaving 10.7 ms, which is very likely ample for submit plus present, so the hard cap of 64 moves from admissible-if toward admissible -- BUT IT DOES NOT MOVE YET, because very likely ample is not a measurement and the entire point of the seed-130 condition was to stop a sim-only number being quoted as a whole-frame number.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_h_n2a_suppress_render_on_catchup SET status='open', text='H-N2a, a falsifiable optimisation hypothesis recorded WITH A STATED PREDICTION THAT IT FAILS, so that it is killed once rather than re-proposed monthly. Because render dispatch, the sprite walker and the NaomiLib submit are INSIDE the timed tick (see finding:supergun_render_budget_unknown), a depth-N rollback re-runs them N times while only the final frame render output is ever displayed; and the shipped game already owns a mechanism for exactly this, since G+0x770 suppresses render on catch-up frames and is how its fast-forward works (rr-ggpo-determinism). HYPOTHESIS: render dispatch can be suppressed on non-final catch-up frames, saving the render fraction of every re-simulated tick and making deep speculation materially cheaper. PRIOR: AGAINST, for a specific reason -- the Gate N1 divergence witness was blk+0x1D6FC = object-pool node 144 field +0x124, A SPRITE-WALKER PLACEMENT FIELD INSIDE blk, so the walker output is rollback state and suppressing it on catch-up frames would change blk and desync. FALSIFICATION, cheap, one ENGINE-lane run: --rollback N with render dispatch suppressed on every catch-up frame except the last; if the resulting blk is not byte-identical to the straight-line state, H-N2a is dead. PREDICTION: IT FAILS. A companion question worth asking in the same run: what fraction of the 0.037 ms tick is render dispatch at all, because if it is 10 percent then H-N2a was never worth much even if true.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_witness_receipt_wording_contract SET status='confirmed', text='W2 MADE COPY-PROOF. The technical fact is unchanged: a save-set hash proves the two peers SIMULATION STATE agreed byte for byte, and cannot prove they DREW THE SAME PIXELS, because submitted geometry lands in the host staging buffer at *(game_state+0x208) which nothing in the pipeline dumps or compares -- demonstrated in RECEIPT-RUNNER-GATE4 s1, where 26 KB of scrambled drawn geometry left ctx_out byte-EQUAL. Because the failure mode is a non-engineer lifting one sentence into a product page, the wording itself is now a contract. NOT APPROVED: provably the same match; pixel-perfect proof; verified frame; we verified the video; cheat-proof; tamper-proof match record. APPROVED: provably the same INPUTS AND GAME STATE verified frame by frame; byte-exact SIMULATION receipt; we re-simulated the match on our own server and it matched byte for byte; any INCONSISTENCY between the two players games is detected; signed replayable record of the inputs and the resulting game state. THE ONE SENTENCE ANYONE MAY COPY: we re-run every match on our own servers from the same inputs and check that the game state matches byte for byte, which proves the two players games agreed -- it is a simulation receipt, not a recording of the video. AND THE LIMIT THAT MUST ACCOMPANY ANY ANTI-CHEAT FRAMING: the witness detects an INCONSISTENT lie and never a CONSISTENT one, so a macro producing frame-perfect but humanly impossible inputs is accepted by both peers and therefore by the witness; server authority would not solve it either; NOTHING HERE MAY BE SOLD AS PREVENTING CHEATING, it detects divergence and produces an auditable record.';

-- edges
RELATE finding:method_check_instrument_health_before_quoting->cites->source:supergun_method_rules_20260904 SET id=cites:m1_src;
RELATE finding:method_seed_replay_failures_are_relate_artefacts->cites->source:supergun_method_rules_20260904 SET id=cites:m2_src;
RELATE finding:method_derived_finding_is_not_independent_confirmation->cites->source:supergun_method_rules_20260904 SET id=cites:m3_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_render_budget_unknown->cites->source:supergun_method_rules_20260904 SET id=cites:un10_rescope_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_h_n2a_suppress_render_on_catchup->cites->source:supergun_method_rules_20260904 SET id=cites:hn2a_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_witness_receipt_wording_contract->cites->source:supergun_method_rules_20260904 SET id=cites:w2_wording_src;
RELATE finding:supergun_witness_receipt_wording_contract->cites->finding:supergun_witness_interface_obligations SET id=cites:w2_wording_from_obligations;
RELATE finding:method_check_instrument_health_before_quoting->cites->finding:supergun_heap_wraps_instrumentation_rule SET id=cites:m1_from_heapwraps;

-- M1 generalises the heap_wraps note; M3 generalises the two dedup notes. Link them so the specific cases point at the rule.
UPDATE finding:supergun_heap_wraps_instrumentation_rule SET note='GENERALISED 2026-09-04 into finding:method_check_instrument_health_before_quoting (rule M1). This node is the specific case that produced the rule; cite the rule for method, this node for the evidence.';
UPDATE finding:supergun_server_authority_ruled_out SET note='NOT AN INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION. This is the SUPERGUN NETCODE lane consumption of finding:supergun_server_authority_loses_on_latency (seed 128, research lane), which is the original and rests on the same arithmetic and the same propagation geometry. Cite ONE of the two, not both, as evidence. What this node adds beyond the original is only the consequence for this lane documents: architecture D is struck from SUPERGUN-NETCODE s3, and Gate N4 is reclassified from a potential architecture discriminator to a measure of absolute transport quality. Governed by rule M3, finding:method_derived_finding_is_not_independent_confirmation.';
UPDATE finding:supergun_pin_and_isolate SET note='NOT AN INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION. This is the SUPERGUN NETCODE lane consumption of finding:supergun_pin_and_isolate_required (seed 128, research lane) and of the single tenancy measurement behind it, finding:supergun_server_tenancy_measured. Cite ONE, not both. What this node adds beyond the original is the SCOPING that the 96 ms figure is a K=32 server-density artefact rather than a client property (at K=1 the max is 0.415 ms), the resulting new open item finding:supergun_client_scheduler_exposure_unknown, and the observation that pinning composes with the s9.8 spin-to-deadline input sampling rather than competing with it. Governed by rule M3, finding:method_derived_finding_is_not_independent_confirmation.';
